    <methods>
      <methodStep>
        <description>
          <para>Input. The full-resolution 1 m bins of the CalCOFI CTD Cast Files, as the calcofi_ctd-cast ingest stages them (obs_ctd_full), for the cast of each station occupation that the ingest publishes in obs (the down cast, the up cast only where no down cast exists). A value the provider flags 8 (questionable) or 9 (bad) is dropped before anything is computed; the temperature and salinity used are the sensor-pair averages the ctd-cast ingest rebuilds by the provider's flags (combine_sensor_pair_sql()).</para>
          <para>Tiers. final and preliminary_with_bottle casts get every product. preliminary_without_bottle casts have no bottle-corrected salinity, so they get only the temperature-criterion mixed-layer depth: nothing salinity-based (spice, sigma-theta, density MLD, geostrophic flow) and no chlorophyll estimate, following Rasmus Swalethorp's rule (2026-09-09) that uncorrected sensors are not shown.</para>
          <para>Spice (spiciness0, kg m-3): absolute salinity from practical salinity (gsw_SA_from_SP), conservative temperature from in-situ temperature (gsw_CT_from_t), then spiciness at 0 dbar (gsw_spiciness0), TEOS-10 via the Gibbs SeaWater toolbox (IOC, SCOR and IAPSO 2010; McDougall and Barker 2011) and McDougall and Krzysik (2015). Positive is spicy (warm, salty), negative minty.</para>
          <para>Averaged sigma-theta (sigma_theta_ave, kg m-3): the two sensors' sigma-theta combined by the provider's flags, the same rule as every CTD pair.</para>
          <para>Mixed-layer depth (m, per cast): the first depth below a 10 m reference where sigma-theta has increased by 0.03 kg m-3 (de Boyer Montegut et al. 2004; mld_sigma_theta_003) or 0.125 kg m-3 (Levitus 1982; mld_sigma_theta_0125), or temperature has departed by 0.2 deg C (de Boyer Montegut et al. 2004; mld_temperature_02), interpolated linearly between the bracketing bins. A cast that never crosses the threshold, or does not reach 10 m, has none.</para>
          <para>Chlorophyll-a maximum (per cast): the depth and value of the maximum of a 5 m running median of the bottle-fitted sensor estimate (est_chlorophyll_a_sta_corr), so a single spiking bin cannot be the maximum.</para>
          <para>Integrated chlorophyll-a (mg m-2, per cast): the trapezoidal integral of the same estimate from the surface to 200 m, or to the cast bottom if shallower (chl_integrated_depth says how deep it reached); the shallowest bin is carried to the surface only when it is no deeper than 5 m.</para>
          <para>Relative geostrophic velocity (m s-1, table ctd_geostrophic): per cruise and CalCOFI line, stations ordered nearshore to offshore, dynamic height anomaly relative to 500 dbar (gsw_geo_strf_dyn_height) on a 1 dbar grid and v = (dh2 - dh1) / (f dx) between adjacent stations, averaged to 10 dbar bins. Positive is equatorward. A station closer than 10 km to the previous one kept is skipped; a pair with a cast shallower than 500 dbar carries its deepest density down and is flagged shallow. It is relative flow, so it has no anomaly.</para>
          <para>Every rule is a function in calcofi4db (ctd_spice(), ctd_sigma_theta_ave(), ctd_mld(), ctd_chl_max(), ctd_integrate(), ctd_geostrophic()) with unit tests. The defaults are awaiting Rasmus Swalethorp's confirmation (questions.csv Q01-Q05).</para>
          <para>References. de Boyer Montegut, C., G. Madec, A. S. Fischer, A. Lazar and D. Iudicone (2004), Mixed layer depth over the global ocean: an examination of profile data and a profile-based climatology, J. Geophys. Res. 109, C12003, doi:10.1029/2004JC002378. Levitus, S. (1982), Climatological Atlas of the World Ocean, NOAA Professional Paper 13. McDougall, T. J. and O. A. Krzysik (2015), Spiciness, J. Mar. Res. 73, 141-152, doi:10.1357/002224015816665589. IOC, SCOR and IAPSO (2010), The international thermodynamic equation of seawater - 2010 (TEOS-10), IOC Manuals and Guides 56. McDougall, T. J. and P. M. Barker (2011), Getting started with TEOS-10 and the Gibbs Seawater (GSW) Oceanographic Toolbox, SCOR/IAPSO WG127. Kelley, D., C. Richards and WG127 (2023), gsw: Gibbs Sea Water Functions, R package.</para>
        </description>
      </methodStep>
    </methods>
